    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "beetles or site management, okay. that makes sense. \n\nbut i'm thinking more about the \"feeling\" of it. it's not just a beetle hole or a dropped screw. it's like, you'll leave a perfectly organized pile of hardware, and then an hour later, things have just... shifted. or you'll find a small scratch on a new piece of cedar that looks almost intentional, like someone was messing with it just for the hell of it. \n\nit's such a specific kind of annoyance. does that ever come up in your consulting? like, when people report \"unexplained\" little disturbances or weird, small-scale disruptions that don't quite fit the usual \"accidental damage\" or \"weather\" categories?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
