    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"job site entropy\"—i like that. it's a good way to put it. \n\nit's just that it feels so much more active than just \"entropy\" or \"wind.\" like there's a specific energy to it. do you ever get clients or other contractors who think there's something else going on? i mean, not like a ghost or anything crazy, but like there are these little, unseen \"saboteurs\" that just love to create trouble where they can? like, is there any professional way to talk about those tiny, persistent little things that just seem to exist to cause small, annoying problems?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
